module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.hold_recovered_by_age_not_observed_holder_death

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data hold_recovered_by_age_not_observed_holder_death: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "hold_recovered_by_age_not_observed_holder_death" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a durable exclusive hold is recovered, lapsed, taken over, or treated as holder death because a declared deadline, RuntimeMaxSec, or grant expiry has passed, rather than because an observer bound to that holder reported HolderObservedDead. std.durable_exclusive_hold durable_hold_recovery_assess admits recovery only on HolderObservedDead keyed to the holder and generation; a declared lease deadline is not that observation. HARM: a live holder inside a slow window is treated as gone (seat, spool, collector session, or capacity grant handed to the next arrival), or a dead holder is treated as gone only because a clock fired, so the recovery does not discriminate death from delay. OPERATOR STANDING (bright-moth-475, 2026-10-12, dashboard msg_3d590516): KEEP the four current sites' behavior; declare each as a typed gap on this row rather than changing recovery to require observed death before the named observers exist.",

    "SITE 1 — compute Reserved launch_deadline (gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle recovery_trigger). In AttemptReserved there is no unit to observe, so now >= record.launch_deadline constructs RecoveryMayTerminate. CURRENT RUNG: mitigatable. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the producer process that opened the reservation becomes a gunbc.process_hold_identity holder, and holder_process_liveness (boot, pid, start time) is the observation recovery_trigger consumes in Reserved; age then cannot fire while that holder is HolderObservedLive or HolderLivenessUnobservable.",

    "SITE 2 — belt RuntimeMaxSec read as death (gunbc.live_deploy.belt_cadence belt_tick_run_bound as systemd RuntimeMaxSec; gunbc.roadmap_belt_actuate belt_exit_running_reconcile_at treating the resulting unit exit as holder death and spooling the attempt). CURRENT RUNG: mitigatable. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the unit observer keyed by InvocationID that gunbc.systemd_unit_invocation_liveness unit_invocation_holder_liveness already names; recovery and exit-reconcile consume HolderObservedDead for that InvocationID, and RuntimeMaxSec is no longer read as death.",

    "SITE 3 — capacity pool lapse_pass (product.capacity.pool lapse_pass). Under std.resource_release_law FencedResource, lease_is_held_and_lapsed_at writes PoolLapsed / Released from expiry alone. CURRENT RUNG: mitigatable. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the resource-side fence — an explicit operator ruling that FencedResource expiry is a legitimate recovery signal for that resource class (the fence itself refuses the stale holder), which retires this site from the class; until that ruling, expiry remains a typed gap even where the law already distinguishes FencedResource from QuiescenceRequired.",

    "SITE 4 — collector takeover on expiry (gunbc.fleet_observation.collector_ownership acquire_ownership). HeldLeaseObservedState LeaseRunningPastExpiry (the expiry-derived arm formerly named LeaseRunningStale; rename-only so it no longer shares Stale with gunbc.session_lease PortObservedStaleExpected fingerprint mismatch) takes over when requested_generation > observed_generation. CURRENT RUNG: mitigatable. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: std.resource_release_law fencing — acquire_ownership takeovers consume a FencedResource / generation fence rather than an expiry-derived observed arm; LeaseRunningPastExpiry then cannot mint OwnershipTakenOver.",

    "SITE 5 - session placement settle pass (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_placement session_placement_settle_pass_at, session_settle_decide, and gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle recovery_trigger's Launching arm). A session worker's seat is a slot in the instance's attempt slot store; in Launching the trigger is OBSERVATIONAL ONLY - the declared launch deadline plays no part - so the seat is kept or released by what the pass can say about the unit, and age cannot be the reason either way. srv1 2026-10-28: lease gunbc-attempt-debt-exclusion-frontier-excludes-nothing-6ea61c671002a6d4.service (head session-memory-srv1.92, slot generation 2, state Launching) reads LoadState=not-found in the system manager AND the user manager, but the instance's attempt-exit spool holds one entry whose name still spells the stop-hook variables unexpanded, and the reader mapped that artifact to UnitLifecycleUnknown, so every pass kept the charge. CURRENT RUNG: mitigatable. WHAT IS ADMISSIBLE AND WHAT IS NOT: a malformed exit artifact is NEVER death proof by itself - it is evidence about its WRITER, and the reader now says so as its own arm (AttemptExitRecordWriterUnsubstituted, minted by attempt_exit_record_matching only when every malformed name for that subject and role spells a stop variable unexpanded; a decodable record still outranks a broken sibling, and an ordinary malformed name is still AttemptExitRecordUnreadable). The same module refuses to WRITE such a name (attempt_exit_record_put_mkdir_name), so the artifact is unwritable through any modeled route. THE FOOTPRINT, MEASURED READ-ONLY ON srv1 ON 2026-10-31: three such entries survive across both roots' spool refused/ stages -- shell-dag-live-deploy-install-owned+9eebe4d74f8a6757+obligation (2026-10-13 03:38Z), v1-interpreter-primitive-dispatch-authority+25de491353dd507f+worker (2026-10-14 21:33Z), debt-exclusion-frontier-excludes-nothing+6ea61c671002a6d4+worker (2026-10-28 06:17Z) -- against 270 entries the exit reader decodes as exits, PLUS 5 entries in those same two done/ stages that are not exits at all: four-part names carrying the literal word handin, a different entry kind with no service result and no process end, which gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_exit_spool attempt_exit_entry_decode refuses as malformed because this revision knows only the seven-part exit shape. A COUNT IS ONLY TRUE OF THE READER THAT PRODUCED IT, and this row's earlier wording counted those 5 hand-ins among the decodable exits -- the very error class this ledger files, sitting in its own receipt. Re-measured read-only on srv1 2026-11-02: current root done/ holds 75 seven-part directories and 3 hand-in files, old root done/ holds 195 directories and 2 hand-in files, so the split is 270 exits, 5 hand-ins, 3 unsubstituted. Each of the 3 unsubstituted entries is a DIRECTORY, the shape a create-only mkdir of the unexpanded name leaves behind; the 5 hand-ins are empty files. So the writer defect spans at least 2026-10-13 to 2026-10-28, crosses the re-root, and hits both the obligation and the worker role: the Oct-14 lease carries the same artifact shape as the Oct-28 one, and neither spool entry can be treated as a one-off. Holder death must be bound to the HOLDER IDENTITY: the manager that ran the unit (the system manager for gunbc-attempt-* units), the boot, and where available the InvocationID. THE ARMS LIVE INSIDE THE OBSERVER AND PRODUCE ITS OWN PROOF TYPE, not a proof beside it: gunbc.systemd_unit_invocation_liveness unit_invocation_holder_liveness (arm a) and unit_reboot_holder_liveness (arm b), each returning DurableHoldHolderLiveness from std.durable_exclusive_hold. (a) THE EXACT-RUN ARM: the run identity recorded at acquisition (manager, boot id, InvocationID) against the observed standing of that same run. (b) THE OBSERVED-REBOOT ARM, for leases whose acquisition recorded no run identity: the current boot's start instant is strictly after the acquisition instant the LEDGER recorded for that lease reference, CONJOINED with not-found read from the manager that ran the unit, AND BOUND TO THE HOLDER'S OWN IDENTITY INSIDE THE ARM: unit_reboot_holder_liveness takes the holder's unit and the manager named for it, and answers HolderLivenessUnobservable when the standing concerns another unit or was read from another manager -- it refuses rather than answering live, because a reading about somebody else does not even establish that this holder is running. A boot fact is a fact about the HOST; it becomes evidence about a holder only conjoined with a reading of that holder's own unit from the manager named for it. No process of a unit started before the current boot survives into it, which is observed death and not age; within the declared clock-skew bound the answer is a typed refusal (UnitBootOrderUndecided), never a release. THE BOOT THAT ORDERS IS THE BOOT THE NOT-FOUND READING CARRIES: UnitInvocationAbsent is { unit, manager, boot_id, boot_started_at }, the order is taken against THAT boot, and the separate boot reading is only a cross-check -- a standing paired with a boot that is not its own is HolderLivenessUnobservable, because two facts never observed together are not one reading. A boot that began BEFORE the acquisition is unobservable, not live: a unit not loaded in a boot that predates the acquisition may never have been started in that boot, and claiming life from absence is the same over-claim as claiming death, in the other direction. THE RUNG, STATED HONESTLY: arm (b) is strictly WEAKER than the InvocationID observer in resolution -- it proves death only across a boot boundary, and never the cause of death -- and it is stronger than nothing at all, which is what the site was before. It is not age: the boot's start instant is an observed host fact, read fresh each pass. WHERE THE CONJUNCTION IS CONSUMED: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_placement session_absent_unit_lifecycle, whose evidence is minted by session_holder_evidence -- the manager named by the recorded launch fact -- the placement record's launch_manager compared with the manager the reading was taken from (roadmap_session_placement session_launch_manager_admissible, branch review 2026-11-07 msg_2b3b7c0c; the prefix rule attempt_unit_manager_is_system is deleted and the two leases whose records predate the field are admitted by value in session_legacy_recorded_manager_absent_references) -- rather than assumed, the boot read from kernel_boot_id_path and proc_stat_path, and the acquisition instant read from the LEDGER by gunbc.compute.host_capacity compute_seat_acquisition_at over gunbc.fabric.fabric_event_log fabric_seat_acquisition_of, keyed on the lease reference. A bare not-found no longer answers at all: session_unit_lifecycle's AttemptUnitAbsent arm is UnitLifecycleUnknown, and the abandonment route (session_placement_abandon) reads the same bound conjunction. THE ARTIFACT ARM ALONE NEVER DISCHARGES, IN EITHER PASS: the settle pass keeps the seat on an unsubstituted artifact read beside a bare not-found standing, and the same artifact beside the BOUND conjunction settles it once. Witnesses: test.claim.roadmap.session_placement_wet_witness an_unsubstituted_exit_artifact_settles_the_real_seat_once_and_the_next_pass_does_nothing (bound) and an_unsubstituted_exit_artifact_with_a_not_found_reading_in_a_boot_that_predates_the_acquisition_keeps_the_seat_and_the_slot (the same fixture, the same artifact, the binding removed), a_not_found_unit_in_the_boot_the_hold_was_acquired_in_keeps_the_seat, a_unit_that_still_reports_an_invocation_id_keeps_the_seat, a_boot_too_close_to_the_acquisition_to_order_keeps_the_seat, a_not_found_unit_with_no_ledger_acquisition_to_bind_to_keeps_the_seat; test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_worker_exit_observation_witness a_gone_unit_without_bound_death_evidence_keeps_the_seat; test.claim.systemd_unit_invocation_liveness_witness boot_and_acquisition_are_ordered_only_outside_the_callers_skew_bound, its three neighbours, and a_foreign_subject_never_frees_the_hold_even_across_a_boot, and a_boot_that_is_not_the_standing_s_own_boot_never_frees_the_hold. REMAINING RUNG: arm (a) waits for acquisition to RECORD the carrier -- gunbc.systemd_unit_invocation_liveness UnitRunIdentity exists (#15460) and nothing writes it into an acquisition yet, so both srv1 leases (2026-10-28 and 2026-10-14) can only be reached by arm (b). THE LIMIT ARM (b) DRAWS ON ITSELF: the ledger-history route (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_placement SettleRetireUncharged, reading gunbc.compute.host_capacity compute_seat_charge_returned) is consulted ONLY where the holder cannot be dated at all, the UnitLifecycleUnknown arm. recovery_trigger's RecoveryUnitNotEnded also covers UnitStillRunning, and an earlier cut of the settle arm matched the keep alone -- which would have closed the slot record of a holder the manager positively reports RUNNING on nothing but a ledger line saying the charge came back. That is this class firing in the opposite direction: the hold is not recovered by age there, but a live holder's only handle would be burned by a bookkeeping act. A charge returned under a live holder is a different defect (a release issued while the holder lived) and the keep now names it instead of retiring. A witness row for that shape -- a_launching_slot_whose_holder_is_observed_alive_is_kept_even_though_the_ledger_already_returned_its_charge -- is in test.claim.roadmap.session_placement_wet_witness and HAS been executed: at head 0c383e8c6fd2, merged as f08a6ae4e44d, claim_batch --wet on that entry answered rc=0 with 10 of 10 rows PASS in 712s on a binary whose gunbc --version equalled that head (PR #15897, the run is recorded on the PR). The keep is an executed fact, not a staged claim.",
    "SITE 6 - the compute door's own not-found reading (gunbc.compute.work_provider_local unit_lifecycle_unpopulated, and unit_termination_unconfirmed, which mints UnitAbsentAuthoritatively from a bare user-manager LoadState=not-found BEFORE it tests attempt_completed; unit_termination_frees_capacity answers true for that arm and is live on the producer's own capacity-return path). This is the EARLIEST site of the class: ebc194893d1e, 2026-09-23, gunbc#12040, the same commit that created the operator door compute_recover_cli, while the placement arm inherited the wording later at 3831be75cb24, 2026-10-03, gunbc#13074. Its guard is vacuous for exactly the unit the reading is about: unit_population maps an empty ControlGroup answer to PopulationUnknown, so the branch that lets an occupied cgroup outrank systemd cannot fire for a dropped unit. It reads the USER manager (gunbc-compute-* are --user transients, and live_deploy.slice_bounds names the user-manager population), and it frees the build pool, not session-memory-<host>, so it is not the route the two srv1 session leases came through. BREADTH, the answer gunbc.design_argument::root_generalization asks of a row that names a sibling site: this site should be generalized, not in this change. The rule belongs at the one predicate both doors already reach, gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle unit_lifecycle_ended, with the manager as a parameter read from a declared row (gunbc-attempt-* is the system manager; gunbc-compute-* and the four other user-side prefixes are the user manager), the terminated arms carrying their authority by construction rather than validated by a guard, and both leaf inferences deleted. TRIGGER, in order: first the compute route gains an exit record of its own (a ComputeUnitStopObservation arm writing the same spool model on a per-launching-user root, because the compute hook runs unprivileged in the user manager and leaves nothing readable behind today), then the generalization. The order is measured, not stylistic, and the instrument is named: classify each release event's reason text in the compute capacity ledger (gunbc.fabric.fabric_event_log terms, read read-only on srv1 on 2026-11-01) against the three renderings of attempt_lifecycle recovery_trigger_wire, and every one of the operator door's 11 historical releases carries the fingerprint of the AttemptLaunching arm - a spawned holder whose producer was gone - so removing the absent arm before the compute route can leave a record would turn 11 working discharges into seats held until the next boot. ITS FIRST TRIGGER IS WRITTEN, NOT YET EXECUTED. The ordering measurement is dated 2026-11-01 (the read-only classification of the operator door's release events on srv1); the record itself lands 2026-11-05 in gunbc#15640, and NO witness entry of this change has been executed at the head this row ships on: the six entries that would execute it (roadmap/roadmap_attempt_exit_spool_witness, roadmap/roadmap_dispatch_actuator_witness, compute/work_request_witness, roadmap/roadmap_belt_actuate_witness, compute_unit_stop_observation_witness, roadmap/attempt_system_unit_launch_witness) are booked for a srv2 window, not run. Everything below therefore describes a WRITTEN state. The executed claim is owed, and until it is paid this site is a model with declared receipts, not a rung recovered by observation - which is the difference this very row exists to keep honest. The compute route has an exit record of its own. gunbc.spool_queue declares SpoolComputeExit with partition ByPrincipalUid and gunbc.compute.host_capacity compute_exit_spool_open is the typed mint that takes the instance plus the principal uid and derives the per-uid path through the one spool_root_dir derivation, owned by instance.directory_owner, so no other uid can plant a record in the spool that frees a seat; gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_exit_spool compute_attempt_exit_hook installs the seat's ExecStopPost writer into that stage through the same install_directory_owned_argv_command the roadmap hook uses, and compute_attempt_exit_record_listing reads it back. The door's stop operand is now a List of the closed ComputeUnitStopObservation coproduct: SccacheStatsAtStop keeps ExecStop, so it still runs before KillMode reaps the sccache server, and AttemptExitRecordAtStop is the ExecStopPost arm; an arm that cannot be rendered refuses the launch as ComputeUnitStopObservationRefused rather than starting a seat whose end nobody will be able to witness. Both folds now issue their freeing arms (UnitAbsentAuthoritatively, UnitTerminatedCauseUnknown) only beside SeatStopRecordFound, the one reading that carries the unit's own invocation id, and None, Unreadable, WriterUnsubstituted, NoUid and NotConsulted each keep the seat; NotConsulted names a ROUTE that opened no spool at all (the manager-only reading the operator door and the belt resolver take), which is a fact about the route and never a seat's end, and it is deliberately not spelled NoUid -- borrowing that name told an operator to fix a uid the process has. The unit a record names is DERIVED by the same declared builder the launcher used (gunbc.systemd_unit_names), never spelled at the write site, and a name no launcher claims is refused by name. The instrument re-runs RED on the recordless reading: dag/test/claim/compute/work_request_witness's four-state row now asserts not-ended where it asserted ended, which is exactly the inference removed - written that way, and shown only by the owed execution above, not by this row's saying so.",

    "THE OCT-28 WRITER IS OUTSIDE WHAT THE SURVIVING ARTIFACTS CAN SHOW, AND THE ROW SAYS SO RATHER THAN NAMING ONE. The placement record on srv1 spells the hook correctly - a single dollar sign before each variable, no shell wrapper; extdeps.systemd.service_exec exec_word_render refuses any literal containing a dollar sign, so a variable spelling can only come from a typed ExecVariable part; extdeps.systemd.systemd_run projects NAME=VALUE verbatim with no escaping and models both the -p and the --property= spellings; and a reproduction on systemd 255.4-1ubuntu8.18 (srv1's version) expands the INVOCATION_ID variable correctly under BOTH spellings. The artifact's name is what systemd leaves when the dollar sign reaching it was protected from the manager's own expansion (a shell wrapper escaping it, or a doubled sign), so the step that produced it sits in a path whose unit was already collected and whose boot's journal is gone - srv1 journalctl --list-boots reaches back only to 2026-10-29 09:17. The reader arm and the put refusal are what the evidence supports; pinning the writer is not.",

    "THE SIBLING srv1 LEASE IS NOT THIS ROW. The 2026-10-14 lease gunbc-attempt-v1-interpreter-primitive-dispatch-authority-25de491353dd507f.service is kept by INVISIBILITY, not by the clock: its slot exists only under the root the WRE-1b re-root (gunb-ai/gunbc#14633, 2026-10-24) abandoned, and the pass enumerates the current declaration's store and nothing else, so no pass can ever see it. Its route is the one-time modeled carry in gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_attempt_slots_cutover: a per-instance declared row naming the instance whose root moved and the root its state was left under, read by attempt_slots_census_for_instance / attempt_slots_carry_for_instance (the census first, with typed unreadable readings and typed counts; the carry keyed on reference plus payload, CAS under ExpectSlotAbsent, idempotent, refusing a different attempt under one reference and refusing a row that names another instance). The carry settles nothing itself - after it, the pass decides on its own evidence. The route is now declared: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate.attempt_slots_cutover_pass runs census then carry for the instance a tick services, in the worker slot lane, and writes what it read into the instance's records directory (the frontier row that pointed at that name was retired when the name landed). The HOST run on srv1 stays gated on its own operator authorization. ONE CONSEQUENCE, MEASURED 2026-11-04: that lease's charge was released in the ledger on 2026-11-04 while its slot was still unreachable, which removed the acquisition instant the holder-death evidence reads (session_holder_evidence refuses when compute_seat_acquisition_at finds no term), so the ordinary close can never fire for it. The settle pass now answers that state with SettleRetireUncharged - the slot taken terminal under the generation read from the slot, no compute_release_on call, and a detail that makes no holder-death claim - because the ledger already returned the charge. A never-acquired slot is NOT retired: the condition is a positive acquisition-then-return in the partition's own history (gunbc.compute.host_capacity compute_seat_charge_returned), never the mere absence of a hold.",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed once each site's named observer (or the FencedResource legitimacy ruling) is the only recovery signal, which is decidable from durable_hold_recovery_assess's coproduct. Until then the class sits at mitigatable: the four sites remain writable and recovery still fires on the clock.",

    "CONSUMPTION: the derived gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster recurring_failure_mode_roster includes this per-class declaration. Behavior at the four sites is unchanged; this row is the census, not a second recovery path.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "std.durable_exclusive_hold", decl_name: "durable_hold_recovery_assess"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "std.durable_exclusive_hold", decl_name: "DurableHoldHolderLiveness"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle", decl_name: "recovery_trigger"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.process_hold_identity", decl_name: "holder_process_liveness"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.live_deploy.belt_cadence", decl_name: "belt_tick_run_bound"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_exit_running_reconcile_at"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.systemd_unit_invocation_liveness", decl_name: "unit_invocation_holder_liveness"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_exit_spool", decl_name: "AttemptExitRecordWriterUnsubstituted"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_exit_spool", decl_name: "attempt_exit_record_matching"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_exit_spool", decl_name: "attempt_exit_record_put_mkdir_name"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.systemd.service_exec", decl_name: "exec_word_render"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.systemd.systemd_run", decl_name: "systemd_run_named_setting_assignment"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_placement", decl_name: "session_worker_unit_lifecycle"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_placement", decl_name: "session_placement_settle_pass_at"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_attempt_slots_cutover", decl_name: "attempt_slots_carry"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_attempt_slots_cutover", decl_name: "attempt_slots_carry_for_instance"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_attempt_slots_cutover", decl_name: "attempt_slots_census_for_instance"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_attempt_slots_cutover", decl_name: "replaced_attempt_slots_roots"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_attempt_slots_cutover", decl_name: "ReplacedAttemptSlotsRootLookup"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_attempt_slots_cutover", decl_name: "AttemptSlotsRowRefusal"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_attempt_slots_cutover", decl_name: "AttemptSlotsSlotReading"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_attempt_slots_cutover", decl_name: "AttemptSlotsCensusCounts"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "attempt_slots_cutover_pass"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_placement", decl_name: "SettleRetireUncharged"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.compute.host_capacity", decl_name: "compute_seat_charge_returned"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_attempt_slots_cutover", decl_name: "attempt_slots_cutover_run_ref"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "product.capacity.pool", decl_name: "lapse_pass"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "std.resource_release_law", decl_name: "FencedResource"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet_observation.collector_ownership", decl_name: "acquire_ownership"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "std.temporal_effect", decl_name: "LeaseRunningPastExpiry"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.session_lease", decl_name: "PortObservedStaleExpected"),
  ],
}
